  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cold front is sitting well offshore, with deep \nlayer nerly flow settling into the majority of ENC. Have\ncontinued decreasing PoPs for the remainder of today and for\ntomorrow. Best moisture will reside acrs the far swrn zones\ntoday, where this area has a 20-30% chance of seeing some\nshowers. High pres in control for Sunday means a drier fcst on \ntap. Next appreciable chance of rain arrives Mon and Tue as yet\nanother frontal boundary pushes southward.\n\nKey Message 2...Next week, a strong high pressure system \nbecomes anchored acrs New England and ern Canada, while at the \nsame time low pres develops off the Mid Atlantic coast, \ntightening the pressure gradient along the mid- atlantic and \nnortheast. This will likely usher in stronger NE winds to the \nregion. Given it is 4-6 days out, there is still much \nuncertainty, as both wind speed and direction is dependent on \nthe placement, strength, and timing of the low. For now there is\ngood model consensus on at least higher waves 8+ ft at 8+ sec \nalong the Outer Banks mid- next week. This will be worth keeping\nan eye on, as a long fetch of strong winds could bring higher \nwave energy towards vulnerable portions of the Outer Banks. It \nis too soon to determine specifics at this point and trends will\nhave to be monitored in the coming days.",
